1
00:00:02,330 --> 00:00:04,460
Stocks and bonds are moving higher...

2
00:00:04,620 --> 00:00:07,130
Why are we watching the Business Channel?

3
00:00:07,290 --> 00:00:11,260
Because the other day I saw there was a stock with my initials, MEG, on it.

4
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:14,430
Sometimes it takes two or three hours before it comes up again.

5
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:17,340
But when it does, it's exciting.

6
00:00:17,510 --> 00:00:21,060
Hmm, okay, honey, you really need a job.

7
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:25,350
Dad says he knows someone you can call for an interview.

8
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:29,230
Right there! That's the third sign today. Right there.

9
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:33,690
On behalf of everyone, I'd just like to say, "Huh?"

10
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:37,660
No, you just said "dad." And everywhere I go today...

11
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:40,450
I keep getting signs telling me to go see my father.

12
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:43,870
Like when I was walking over here and I passed a buffet.

13
00:00:45,870 --> 00:00:47,330
Which is my father's last name.

14
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:49,250
Ah.

15
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:51,210
And they were serving franks...

16
00:00:51,380 --> 00:00:53,920
which is his first name, minus the "s" at the end.

17
00:00:54,090 --> 00:00:55,670
- Yes.     - All right.

18
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:59,680
And there was a rotisserie with a spinning chicken.

19
00:00:59,850 --> 00:01:02,470
His Indian name?

20
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:07,140
No. Because I chickened out the last time...

21
00:01:07,850 --> 00:01:11,360
when I tried to meet him. So coincidences? I don't think so.

22
00:01:11,570 --> 00:01:13,860
- Very freaky.     - Eerie.

23
00:01:14,070 --> 00:01:15,780
Who wants the last hamburger?

24
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:18,110
That's it. Now I have to go see him, ha, ha.

25
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:19,410
Why?

26
00:01:19,570 --> 00:01:22,830
Hamburger? McDonald's?

27
00:01:22,990 --> 00:01:25,910
Old McDonald had a farm. My dad is a pharmacist.

28
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:27,830
Ah.

29
00:01:33,140 --> 00:01:37,670
∮ So no one told you life was gonna be this way ∮

30
00:01:38,210 --> 00:01:42,380
∮ Your job's a joke, you're broke, your love life's D.O.A. ∮

31
00:01:43,290 --> 00:01:47,100
∮ It's like you're always stuck in second gear ∮

32
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:49,660
∮ When it hasn't been your day, ∮

33
00:01:49,660 --> 00:01:52,660
∮ your week, your month, or even your year ∮

34
00:01:52,660 --> 00:01:56,620
∮ but I'll be there for you ∮

35
00:01:56,620 --> 00:01:58,450
∮ When the rain starts to pour ∮

36
00:01:58,450 --> 00:02:01,570
∮ I'll be there for you ∮

37
00:02:01,570 --> 00:02:03,410
∮ Like I've been there before ∮

38
00:02:03,410 --> 00:02:06,420
∮ I'll be there for you ∮

39
00:02:06,420 --> 00:02:10,080
∮ 'Cause you're there for me too ∮

40
00:02:15,170 --> 00:02:16,420
Man, I am so beat.

41
00:02:16,590 --> 00:02:18,170
Oh, yeah.

42
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:20,630
You wanna forget racquetball and hang out?

43
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:22,390
Yeah, all right.

44
00:02:25,430 --> 00:02:28,810
- Hey, you're in our seats.     - Oh, sorry, we didn't know.

45
00:02:28,980 --> 00:02:30,640
Hey, we were sitting there.

46
00:02:30,850 --> 00:02:33,980
Okay. There is one more way to say it.

47
00:02:34,150 --> 00:02:35,860
- Who knows it? Ha, ha.     - Ha, ha.

48
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:42,070
- Is that supposed to be funny?     - Actually, I was going for colorful.

49
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:43,990
- What's with this guy?     - What's with you?

50
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:46,740
Uh, nothing. Nothing's with him.

51
00:02:46,910 --> 00:02:48,370
Enjoy your coffee.

52
00:02:55,340 --> 00:02:57,000
What just happened?

53
00:02:58,380 --> 00:03:00,470
I just took your hat.

54
00:03:00,970 --> 00:03:01,960
See, I can be funny too.

55
00:03:02,010 --> 00:03:05,100
My joke is that I took your hat.

56
00:03:05,260 --> 00:03:07,640
That is funny.

57
00:03:08,390 --> 00:03:09,640
Can I have it back?

58
00:03:09,850 --> 00:03:10,980
No.

59
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:14,150
- No?     - No.

60
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:16,770
Okay. Okay.

61
00:03:18,190 --> 00:03:20,860
You know what? I think you're very funny.

62
00:03:21,030 --> 00:03:23,950
Kudos on that hat joke. Ha, ha.

63
00:03:25,910 --> 00:03:28,990
But come on, guys, just give him back the hat.

64
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:31,460
Why should we?

65
00:03:31,620 --> 00:03:33,870
Because it's a special hat.

66
00:03:34,750 --> 00:03:37,590
He bought it because he was feeling down one day.

67
00:03:37,750 --> 00:03:39,130
So he got the hat...

68
00:03:39,300 --> 00:03:41,470
to cheer himself up, you know?

69
00:03:41,630 --> 00:03:45,550
- Now, Chandler...     - Stop talking. Stop talking now.

70
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:49,640
Let me get this straight. You're stealing my hat?

71
00:03:49,810 --> 00:03:50,890
You got a problem?

72
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:53,770
I just want to make sure we're on the same page.

73
00:03:56,770 --> 00:03:58,480
How'd the interview go?

74
00:03:58,690 --> 00:03:59,980
It bit.

75
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:03,320
It was a '50s theme restaurant.

76
00:04:03,490 --> 00:04:07,070
I'd have to cook in a costume and dance on the counter.

77
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:09,580
I was a sous-chef at Café des Artistes.

78
00:04:09,740 --> 00:04:14,290
How can I take a job where I have to make Laverne-and-Curly Fries?

79
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:16,790
- Don't do it.     - How can I not do it?

80
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:18,790
I have $127 in the bank.

81
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:22,010
Monica, relax. Go get a beer.

82
00:04:22,170 --> 00:04:23,510
I don't want a beer.

83
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,130
Who said it was for you?

84
00:04:30,970 --> 00:04:32,770
Hi.

85
00:04:33,850 --> 00:04:35,140
What's the matter?

86
00:04:35,310 --> 00:04:38,520
Some mean guys at the coffeehouse took my hat.

87
00:04:38,730 --> 00:04:40,440
- No.     - You're kidding.

88
00:04:40,650 --> 00:04:43,070
It was ridiculous. These guys were bullies.

89
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:45,200
Actual bullies.

90
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:48,200
We're grownups. This kind of stuff isn't supposed to happen anymore.

91
00:04:48,370 --> 00:04:50,620
- Oh, hi.     - Hi.

92
00:04:50,830 --> 00:04:52,240
Oh...

93
00:04:52,410 --> 00:04:55,040
Oh, no, wait a minute. I have no one.

94
00:04:58,750 --> 00:05:01,460
Let's go down there and get your hat back.

95
00:05:01,630 --> 00:05:05,840
Forget it. It's probably stripped and sold for parts by now.

96
00:05:07,300 --> 00:05:09,890
- Hey. I went up!     - What?

97
00:05:10,050 --> 00:05:13,430
My stock, MEG, it went up two points.

98
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:17,850
Do you realize that if I'd invested my $127 in myself yesterday...

99
00:05:18,020 --> 00:05:21,730
that I'd, like, have a lot more than that today.

100
00:05:23,070 --> 00:05:24,820
You know what? I'm gonna do it.

101
00:05:25,740 --> 00:05:28,030
- Do what?     - Put all my money in me.

102
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:31,070
You don't know a thing about the stock market.

103
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:34,200
What's to know? Buy, sell. High, low. Bears, bulls.

104
00:05:34,370 --> 00:05:36,250
Yes, Manhattan.

105
00:05:36,620 --> 00:05:38,710
Telephone number to the stock...

106
00:05:39,290 --> 00:05:41,130
selling store.

107
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:54,430
See? Didn't I tell you these pillows would be a good idea?

108
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:56,890
Oh, God.

109
00:05:57,060 --> 00:05:58,890
Here we go.

110
00:05:59,060 --> 00:06:02,980
For the first time in my life, I'm gonna say, "Hi, birth father!"

111
00:06:03,650 --> 00:06:05,820
- We love you. We're here for you.     - Good luck.

112
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:07,070
Thanks.

113
00:06:10,950 --> 00:06:12,620
Hey, Rach, you, uh, want some sandwich?

114
00:06:12,780 --> 00:06:15,120
Oh, what is in that?

115
00:06:15,290 --> 00:06:17,500
Olive loaf and ham spread. No mayo.

116
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:20,580
No, because mayo, that would make it gross.

117
00:06:20,790 --> 00:06:24,500
Hey, hey... No, oh, oh, oh.

118
00:06:24,710 --> 00:06:27,300
- Run, Phoebe, run.     - No, no, doggy, please!

119
00:06:27,470 --> 00:06:31,090
I do so want to love all animals. Please, no. Back off!

120
00:06:31,260 --> 00:06:33,430
- You got a bone?     - Are you kidding?

121
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:35,720
Look, kibbles! Bits, oh!

122
00:06:37,180 --> 00:06:39,940
Get the hell off my leg, you yippity piece of crap!

123
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:45,730
Ooh.

124
00:06:47,030 --> 00:06:49,440
Okay. All right. We have a problem.

125
00:06:50,030 --> 00:06:52,490
Why don't you take his trampoline?

126
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:54,830
Okay, here, I know what we can do.

127
00:06:54,990 --> 00:06:57,370
Hey. Hey. Hey, no!

128
00:06:57,540 --> 00:07:00,960
Okay, doggy, get the sandwich! Aah!

129
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:04,630
Go get the sandwich! Good doggy. Get the sandwich!

130
00:07:05,170 --> 00:07:08,920
The dog will lick himself but he will not touch your sandwich.

131
00:07:09,090 --> 00:07:10,590
What does that tell you?

132
00:07:11,970 --> 00:07:14,140
- Lf he's not gonna eat it, I will.     - Are you crazy?

133
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:18,100
Pheebs, he's just a little dog. Aah!

134
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:25,900
- Hey.     - What?

135
00:07:26,070 --> 00:07:28,530
Do you have to be a Century 21 real-estate agent...

136
00:07:28,690 --> 00:07:31,740
to get to wear those cool jackets?

137
00:07:33,780 --> 00:07:36,580
Do you say this stuff to girls?

138
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:42,330
Hey, isn't that the guy who used to wear your hat?

139
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:44,330
And look where they're sitting.

140
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:51,720
You're joking, right? You guys just walked through the door.

141
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:54,180
- Maybe we didn't make it clear enough.     - Yeah.

142
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:57,050
This couch belongs to us.

143
00:07:57,220 --> 00:08:00,770
I'll tell you what, you call the couch...

144
00:08:00,930 --> 00:08:03,270
and then we'll call the couch...

145
00:08:04,940 --> 00:08:06,520
and we'll see who it comes to.

146
00:08:08,150 --> 00:08:11,860
You know what I keep wondering? Why you two are still sitting here.

147
00:08:12,070 --> 00:08:13,820
All right, that's it.

148
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:16,030
I have had enough of this, all right?

149
00:08:16,530 --> 00:08:17,620
Gunther.

150
00:08:18,870 --> 00:08:20,990
These guys are trying to take our seat.

151
00:08:22,790 --> 00:08:25,170
Fellas, these guys were here first.

152
00:08:25,370 --> 00:08:27,210
- Oh, sorry, didn't realize.     - Ahem.

153
00:08:27,420 --> 00:08:28,710
There you go.

154
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:31,170
Thank you, Gunther.

155
00:08:33,970 --> 00:08:35,800
We didn't want to have to go and do that.

156
00:08:37,090 --> 00:08:39,510
He told on us?

157
00:08:39,760 --> 00:08:40,930
You told on us?

158
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:44,390
Well, pal, you didn't give me much of a choice.

159
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:48,400
- Don't play with his thing.     - I know.

160
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:52,150
All right.

161
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:54,860
Let's take this outside.

162
00:08:56,490 --> 00:08:59,740
"Let's take this outside"?

163
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:04,500
Who talks like that?

164
00:09:04,710 --> 00:09:09,130
The guy who's about to kick your ass talks like that.

165
00:09:09,290 --> 00:09:11,670
- You had to ask.     - Yeah.

166
00:09:14,630 --> 00:09:17,050
Okay, okay, look. See...

167
00:09:17,220 --> 00:09:21,350
the thing is, we're not gonna fight you guys.

168
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:23,680
Here's the deal.

169
00:09:23,850 --> 00:09:28,850
You won't have to, so long as you never ever show your faces here again.

170
00:09:34,110 --> 00:09:37,150
I think you played the Gunther card too soon.

171
00:09:43,370 --> 00:09:45,580
Hey, Pheebs, I think you're good to go.

172
00:09:45,790 --> 00:09:47,540
Yeah, I don't know.

173
00:09:49,540 --> 00:09:50,630
What's the matter?

174
00:09:50,790 --> 00:09:53,300
I just think that this was a really bad sign.

175
00:09:53,460 --> 00:09:56,970
Like the beast at the threshold.

176
00:09:58,430 --> 00:10:03,350
It's just I have no family left, except for my grandmother.

177
00:10:03,510 --> 00:10:06,470
But let's face it, she's not gonna be around forever.

178
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:08,100
Despite what she says.

179
00:10:09,730 --> 00:10:15,860
And I have a sister who I've barely spoken to since we shared a womb.

180
00:10:16,030 --> 00:10:18,190
I don't know. This is my real father...

181
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:21,200
and I want things to be, like, just right.

182
00:10:21,370 --> 00:10:23,240
I completely understand.

183
00:10:23,410 --> 00:10:24,990
Yeah, whatever you need.

184
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:28,290
Hey, you want to go home?

185
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:30,790
Okay, thanks. Sorry again.

186
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:52,060
What was that?

187
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:59,240
Uh, I'm guessing the threshold's clear now.

188
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:05,490
I want to buy five shares of SGJ. Now.

189
00:11:05,660 --> 00:11:08,200
Come on, time is money, my friend!

190
00:11:08,370 --> 00:11:11,160
Thank you! Whoo!

191
00:11:11,330 --> 00:11:13,290
"Time is money, my friend"?

192
00:11:13,500 --> 00:11:15,170
You missed "Takes money to make money"...

193
00:11:15,380 --> 00:11:20,090
and "Don't make me come down there and kick your Wall Street butt."

194
00:11:20,300 --> 00:11:23,840
I made $17 before breakfast. What have you done?

195
00:11:24,050 --> 00:11:27,640
I had breakfast here, so technically I saved $3.50.

196
00:11:29,100 --> 00:11:30,560
How did you make $17?

197
00:11:30,770 --> 00:11:33,060
Well, my financially challenged friends...

198
00:11:33,230 --> 00:11:36,650
I split my money and I bought some shares of CHP and ZXY.

199
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:38,730
How come those?

200
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:43,700
Well, CHP because I used to have a crush on Erik Estrada.

201
00:11:44,660 --> 00:11:48,740
And ZXY because I think it sounds "zexy."

202
00:11:48,950 --> 00:11:51,080
Ahem, what happened to MEG?

203
00:11:51,290 --> 00:11:53,710
MEG was good for me, but I dumped her.

204
00:11:53,870 --> 00:11:57,340
My motto is, "Get out before they go down."

205
00:11:58,420 --> 00:12:01,050
That is so not my motto.

206
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:07,640
- Hey.     - Hey, Pheebs.

207
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:09,060
Oh, hey, how's the dog?

208
00:12:09,220 --> 00:12:12,930
Okay. I talked to the vet. People are so nice upstate.

209
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:16,600
He said the little fella's gonna be okay, and I can get him tomorrow.

210
00:12:16,810 --> 00:12:18,400
- Good.     - Oh, thank God.

211
00:12:18,570 --> 00:12:20,820
But he did have to have a bunch of stitches.

212
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:24,700
And he said that only once in a blue moon does a dog's ear grow back.

213
00:12:24,860 --> 00:12:29,030
So still hoping.

214
00:12:30,830 --> 00:12:35,620
Now are you gonna call your dad to let him know that his dog is okay?

215
00:12:35,830 --> 00:12:39,590
I don't want to meet my father over the phone.

216
00:12:39,750 --> 00:12:42,260
What will I say, "Hi, I'm the daughter you abandoned.

217
00:12:42,420 --> 00:12:45,090
Oh, by the way, I broke your dog."

218
00:12:46,050 --> 00:12:48,720
Hey, Pheebs, if you want, I'll do it.

219
00:12:48,930 --> 00:12:50,010
Okay.

220
00:12:50,560 --> 00:12:54,180
Listen, just don't say anything about me, okay?

221
00:12:54,890 --> 00:12:56,100
Don't...

222
00:12:58,110 --> 00:12:59,360
be too long with the phone.

223
00:13:00,520 --> 00:13:04,320
She'll be a much better friend once the market closes.

224
00:13:06,860 --> 00:13:07,950
It's a woman.

225
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:09,570
So talk to her.

226
00:13:12,540 --> 00:13:14,500
Uh, hello, Mrs. Buffay.

227
00:13:16,250 --> 00:13:18,670
I know where your dog is.

228
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:22,710
I want you to know he'll be returned to you almost as good as new...

229
00:13:22,880 --> 00:13:25,380
within 24 hours.

230
00:13:25,550 --> 00:13:27,760
Uh, goodbye.

231
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:36,600
- Why the voice?     - Hard to say.

232
00:13:40,310 --> 00:13:41,610
Your cappuccino, sir.

233
00:13:41,770 --> 00:13:43,440
Thank you.

234
00:13:46,450 --> 00:13:50,450
- This is better than the coffeehouse.     - Absolutely.

235
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,380
How come it's not mixing with the water?

236
00:14:01,540 --> 00:14:04,090
The package says to keep it moving.

237
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:06,800
Stir and drink, never let it settle.

238
00:14:12,140 --> 00:14:14,100
This is ridiculous.

239
00:14:14,310 --> 00:14:17,020
After I get back from my niece's christening...

240
00:14:17,180 --> 00:14:21,690
I'll go to the coffeehouse with you and we'll have a cup of coffee.

241
00:14:21,860 --> 00:14:24,320
No problem. Joey's there, hmm?

242
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:27,400
- Okay.     - No.

243
00:14:28,150 --> 00:14:29,280
- No?     - No.

244
00:14:29,450 --> 00:14:34,410
I don't want to have to have Joey with me every time I want decent coffee.

245
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:38,080
And I don't want to drink cappuccino with a "k."

246
00:14:38,250 --> 00:14:41,460
I say you and I go and stand up to those guys.

247
00:14:41,670 --> 00:14:44,090
All right, hang on a second there, Custer.

248
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:48,130
Ross, have you ever been beaten up before?

249
00:14:48,300 --> 00:14:49,340
Yeah, sure.

250
00:14:49,510 --> 00:14:52,680
- By someone besides Monica?     - No.

251
00:14:53,680 --> 00:14:54,760
So what?

252
00:14:54,930 --> 00:14:58,430
So we get beaten up. Maybe that's something a man has to go through.

253
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:01,900
Like a rite of passage or something.

254
00:15:02,060 --> 00:15:05,230
Couldn't we just lose our virginities again?

255
00:15:06,230 --> 00:15:09,110
Because I think actually mine's growing back.

